# Pre-order delay email + customer name casing (learned 2026-10-05)

Owner-approved delay notice tone (Emma Kim / ORD-muuv8629 sample). Signature + confidentiality stay in transactional branding — do not duplicate Kind regards / address block in the HTML body.

## Delay email structure (`buildPreorderDelayEmailHtml`)

1. Dear {Title Case name},
2. Thank you for your patience… update regarding estimated dispatch date…
3. Reason paragraph — default: international transit and customs delays (see `MARKET_S_PREORDER_DELAY_DEFAULT_REASON`). Admin optional note **replaces** the default reason.
4. **Updated Ship Date** block: Order ID, Pre-order Item(s), Previous Ship Date, New Ship Date
5. AusPost transit starts after dispatch (on or after updated date), not from payment date
6. Apology + reply / info@selpic.com.au

## Customer names in emails

Use `formatCustomerDisplayName` / `resolveOrderCustomerGreetingName` (`lib/formatCustomerDisplayName.ts`).

| Input | Greeting |
|---|---|
| `EMMA kim` / `emma KIM` | `Emma Kim` |
| Missing name, email `emma.kim@…` | `Emma Kim` |
| Empty | `Customer` (inbound drafts: `there`) |

**Do** Title Case personal names on Dear lines (confirmation, deposit confirmed, delay, inbound drafts, document/invoice personal billing names).

**Do not** Title Case company billing names (keep `billing.companyName` as entered). Do not invent Mc*/Mac* special cases unless asked.

